<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Ceratopteris richardii Schnakenberg wavelength at 256 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Ceratopteris richardii)",
        "Ceratopteris richardii Schnakenberg wavelength at 256 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Ceratopteris richardii morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ceratopteris richardii specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Ceratopteris richardii" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Ceratopteris pigment was shown experimentally to obey these rate constants.",
        "does_not_claim: That a fossil chronospecies at 512 µm was measured. The series has one node, Holocene 0 Ma.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Pass-1 GIF matches the plate. CV similarity is 65.9.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The rendered activator is initialized on that critical mode plus seed-3143 noise.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: gamma is solved so k_c = 2*pi/256 µm on a 768 µm periodic window at age 0 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Geng, Yan and Zhou 2022 and Bartz and Gola 2018 describe the Ceratopteris notch meristem and archegonium positions. They do not publish a 256 µm pigment wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979 select a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor out-diffuses the activator.",
        "transfer_boundary: Applying Schnakenberg kinetics to the gallery primordium plate is a scale assignment, not a measurement from the fern papers." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Ceratopteris richardii" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Ceratopteris" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/ceratopteris_richardii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Ceratopteris richardii; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979 select a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor out-diffuses the activator. | Geng, Yan and Zhou 2022 and Bartz and Gola 2018 describe the Ceratopteris notch meristem and archegonium positions. They do not publish a 256 µm pigment wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma is solved so k_c = 2*pi/256 µm on a 768 µm periodic window at age 0 Ma. | The rendered activator is initialized on that critical mode plus seed-3143 noise.; transfer_boundary: Applying Schnakenberg kinetics to the gallery primordium plate is a scale assignment, not a measurement from the fern papers.; does_not_claim: That Ceratopteris pigment was shown experimentally to obey these rate constants. | That a fossil chronospecies at 512 µm was measured. The series has one node, Holocene 0 Ma. | That the Pass-1 GIF matches the plate. CV similarity is 65.9.]; phenomenon_size: 214 µm (0.000214 m, log10=-3.67 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 214 µm to 32.4 cm): 214 µm:ceratopteris-richardii-bioelectric-polarity, 756 µm:ceratopteris-richardii-vertex-packing, 7.2 mm:ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength, 2.6 cm:ceratopteris-richardii-clock-wavefront, 4.5 cm:ceratopteris-richardii-morphogen-condensation, 5.8 cm:ceratopteris-richardii-flux-canalization, 6.3 cm:ceratopteris-richardii-elastic-buckling, 7.5 cm:ceratopteris-richardii-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2018.10.005>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-022-03627-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/297255>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
